trace what a canvas frame spends

Two questions the 0052 trace could not answer. The shelf sitting still was
never taken as unchanged, so 0052's skip never ran, and nothing said what
moved. And the cart animations ran 12-24 ms of draw_list a frame, which
the one-in-sixty sprite profile never caught.

Measurement only, behind the same profiling switch as the rest of the
soft: lines:

- at most once a second, when a canvas frame with no game is not a repeat
  of the last: a texture change, which of gain, shake, slide or screen
  moved and from what to what, the list's length changing, or the first
  item that differs, before and after;
- for a canvas frame whose draw_list ran over 12 ms, its three slowest
  draws: kind, size drawn, texture size, ms.

Test: the slowest draws come out slowest first, a full-canvas texture
ahead of a label.

Applies on top of 0052, upstream 91499a9.

